  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18201",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** a \"Recommended for You\" carousel displayed across relevant pages of the site, \n\n**so that** I can discover products tailored to my browsing and purchase history.\n\n----\n\nThis story covers the PWA build of the Recommended for You component across two surfaces: the PDP and the search overlay (both empty/zero-query state and autocomplete/search-in-progress state). The cart surface is covered separately in [SFCC-815](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-815).\n\nRecommendations are powered by Einstein Product Recommendations with rules-based fallback. For logged-in shoppers, recommendations are driven by behavioural and purchase history data; for guests, fallback is session-based browsing history.\n\nThe component renders using the Product Card Group component ( [SFCC-743](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-743) ), which controls layout, header display, and product card rendering. Quick-add to bag (bag icon on tile hover) is part of the final design and is inherited from the standard product tile — the PDP reference images below show an earlier design state without the bag icons.\n\nThe component can be built and unit tested independently. Integration testing on each surface depends on the host pages being delivered by Squad A: PDP ( [SFCC-5](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-5) ) and Search Autocomplete ( [SFCC-114](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-114) ). Einstein zone configuration is a prerequisite — see [SFCC-112](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-112).\n\n**Reference Images (Figma is leading):**\n\n**PDP ** note that the bag icons should be displayed for Recommended for You products:*\n\n![\"image-20260803-231622.png\"](image-20260803-231622.png)\n\n**Search autocomplete:**\n\n![\"image-20260831-064004.png\"](image-20260831-064004.png)",
