  "description": "**As a** Developer,\n\n**I want** to review the current product attribute structure and filtering capabilities, and research Salesforce Einstein's recommendation engine and its filtering configuration options,\n\n**so that** the team has a clear understanding of what's technically available before designing the product listing, search, and recommendation features.\n\n----\n\n## Scope of work\n\n- Review existing/planned product attributes (e.g. size, color, category, price, custom attributes) and how they map to filtering functionality on PLP/Search\n- Document current filtering capabilities and any technical constraints or limitations\n- Research SFCC Einstein recommendation capabilities (e.g. product recommendations, personalization, merchandising strategies)\n- Investigate Einstein's filtering/configuration options (e.g. how recommendations can be scoped or filtered by attribute, category, or business rule)\n- Identify any gaps between business requirements and out-of-the-box Einstein/filtering capabilities\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n-   Product attributes and their filtering behavior are documented\n-   Einstein recommendation capabilities are documented with supported use cases\n-   Einstein filtering/configuration options are documented\n-   Any technical gaps or limitations are flagged for discussion with the Product Owner/BA\n-   Findings are shared with the team (e.g. via Confluence page or team sync)",
