  "summary": "Product Card Shared Component",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18432",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** product cards to display relevant information for the surface I am browsing, \n\n**so that** each page feels appropriately tailored without inconsistent component implementations across the site.\n\n----\n\n**Images for reference (Figma is leading):**\n\n![\"image-20260727-234551.png\"](image-20260727-234551.png)\n\n\n\nThis story covers the build of a single shared Product Card component that supports multiple display variations via a style prop. Each variation controls which elements are shown — the component itself is built and maintained once. The component is scoped to the visual and interactive layer only — product data is sourced from SFCC. \n\n**Variations in scope:** \n\n- Homepage\n- PLP\n- Wish List\n- Recently Viewed",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready for QA",
    "category": "In Progress",
