{"result":"{
  "id": "19339",
  "key": "SFCC-834",
  "summary": "recommended-for-you",
  "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable `recommended-for-you` React component built to the Zimmermann Design System 2026 spec, so that it can render a labelled, horizontally scrollable image-only product tile carousel on the Cart page.\n\n----\n\nThe component renders a heading and a row of product image tiles. It does not own the recommendation data or navigation logic — it receives a product array, title, and configuration props from the parent. It is shared across two cart surfaces: Recommended For You (title = \"RECOMMENDED FOR YOU\") and Shop the Look (title = \"SHOP THE LOOK\"). Each tile is clickable and navigates to the product's PDP. Minimum tile count is 2; maximum is 10.\n\nProps in scope:\n\n|Prop|Values|Notes|\n|---|---|---|\n|size|Large, Small|Controls tile dimensions; does not affect tile count|\n|showScroll|true, false|Toggles scroll progress indicator; Large only|\n|showImage3|true, false|Toggles 3rd tile|\n|showImage4|true, false|Toggles 4th tile|\n|showImage5|true, false|Toggles 5th tile|\n|showImage6|true, false|Toggles 6th tile|\n|showImage7|true, false|Toggles 7th tile|\n|showImage8|true, false|Toggles 8th tile|\n|showImage9|true, false|Toggles 9th tile|\n|showImage10|true, false|Toggles 10th tile|\n|title|string|Section heading text e.g. \"RECOMMENDED FOR YOU\", \"SHOP THE LOOK\"|",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready For Review",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Dani Rivett",
    "name": "Dani Rivett",
    "email": null,
    "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/42d3d7910c25b8f4ba9e46aabfc6c149?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDR-3.png"
  },
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "Size\n\n# Given size=Large, when the component renders, then tiles display at the Large dimension per the Figma spec.\n# Given size=Small, when the component renders, then tiles display at the Small dimension per the Figma spec.\n\nScroll indicator\n\n# Given size=Large and showScroll=true, when more than 3 products are provided, then a horizontal scroll progress indicator is displayed beneath the tiles.\n# Given size=Large and showScroll=false, when the component renders, then no scroll progress indicator is displayed.\n# Given size=Small, when the component renders, then no scroll progress indicator is displayed regardless of the showScroll value.\n\nTile count\n\n# Given showImage3=true, when the component renders, then a 3rd tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage4=true, when the component renders, then a 4th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage5=true, when the component renders, then a 5th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage6=true, when the component renders, then a 6th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage7=true, when the component renders, then a 7th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage8=true, when the component renders, then an 8th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage9=true, when the component renders, then a 9th tile is displayed.\n# Given showImage10=true, when the component renders, then a 10th tile is displayed.\n# Given all showImage props are false, when the component renders, then exactly 2 tiles are displayed.\n# Given the component is rendered with an empty or missing product array, when it mounts, then no tiles are rendered and no error is thrown.\n\nTitle\n\n# Given a title prop is provided, when the component renders, then the heading is displayed in uppercase per the Design System spec.\n\nInteraction\n\n# Given a shopper clicks a product tile, when the action completes, then they are navigated to that product's PDP.\n\nLayout\n\n# Given the component is rendered on desktop, when it mounts, then the layout matches the Figma spec